macOS 27 (2026-11-22): trackpad, root disk as disk0 for Disk Arbitration, UFS health, trackpad haptics.

- SweetHID: the touchscreen as a trackpad (sweetpad, default 1): one finger moves, tap clicks, tap-and-slide drags,
  two fingers scroll, two-finger tap right-clicks, three fingers hold the button and drag (windows by the title bar).
  Haptic click on clicks and drag starts (sysctl kern.sweet_pad_haptic_gain/_wave, default waveform 10 at 0x80;
  boot-arg sweetpadhaptic). Pointer release at the last finger position; press sent after a move-only event.
- IOHIDEvent: number changed buttons in pointer events (right click was reported as button 1), macOS only.
- sweet_haptic: sweet_haptic_tick() plays a waveform from a thread call (macOS).
- SweetMedia: IOBlockStorageDevice stand-in parent and IOMediaIcon (DADiskCreateFromIOMedia needs both).
- sweet_ufs / IOKitBSDInit: on macOS the root disk is only disk0 / rdisk0 and is mounted as /dev/disk0 (hfs.util -p
  takes only "disk..." names; with two names Disk Arbitration tried to mount the root again and login hung);
  the iOS "disk0" placeholder nub is left out on macOS. The UFS Health Descriptor is read once at start
  (sysctl kern.sweet_ufs_health).

